<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Guanjuato state to build $830m railroad.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Guanjuato state to build $830m railroad.</headline>
<dateline>LEON, Mexico 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Mexico's central Guanajuato state said on Monday that it plans to begin work next year on a railroad linking its main industrial cities.</p>
<p>&quot;The project is a three-year project and will cost about $830 million,&quot; the state's public works chief Cristobal Ascencio told reporters.</p>
<p>Mexican builder Empresas ICA, Canadian firms Bombardier and GMAT, and Germany's Siemens are the four private firms that will build the railway, government officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are talking about at least $550 million during the first stage ... it's very likely that construction will begin in 1997. We are only waiting for the bank credits to be approved,&quot; Ascencio told reporters.</p>
<p>The train will connect the industrial zones of the cities of Celaya, Irapuato, Leon, Guanajuato and Salamanca.</p>
<p>-- David Monjarraz, Leon bureau +5247 161-225</p>
</text>
